  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A$ be the point of intersection of the lines $L_1: \\frac{x-7}{1}=\\frac{y-5}{0}=\\frac{z-3}{-1}$ and $L_2: \\frac{x-1}{3}=\\frac{y+3}{4}=\\frac{z+7}{5}$. Let $B$ and $C$ be the point on the lines $L_1$ and $L_2$ respectively such that $\\mathrm{AB}=\\mathrm{AC}=\\sqrt{15}$. Then the square of the area of the triangle ABC is :",
    "image": null
  },
